index 0000000..697706b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/unreleased/2026-11-26-gpu-when-seen.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+- Windows: a CPU-first window makes its GPU only once it is in sight. Minimized, hidden or covered whole, it stays on the CPU renderer with no device (a failed try's retry waits too) and starts the GPU on the first idle turn it shows again. `App::open_minimized` shows the window's first open minimized and inactive, as a login item started minimized does: its first frame is painted on the CPU while it is hidden and copied whole when the window is restored, and no GPU is made until then. A translucent window, and one that opens maximized or full screen, opens as before.
